              "type": "text",
              "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.895,
            0.12,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "186"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.085,
            0.883,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "wear the dress that you used to wear four years ago? No, because you have become larger in size. This is due to "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "growth",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in your body. Plants and other living beings also grow. Can we consider growth as a characteristic of living beings?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.167,
            0.883,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Living beings need food ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "nutrition",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ") for their growth and development. List five living beings that require food to grow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.228,
            0.884,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, think of a process without which we cannot live. Count the number of breaths you take per minute after a normal walk, after a run, and after a few dance steps. Record the data and observe. Do you notice any difference in the number of breaths after each situation? Do you notice the process of breathing in other animals like dogs, cats, cows and buffaloes? Notice the movement of their abdomen while they are taking rest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.392,
            0.884,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the process of breathing, when we inhale, the air moves from outside to inside our body. When we breathe out, the air moves from inside our body to outside. Breathing is part of a process called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "respiration",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Do plants also respire? There are tiny pores called stomata on the surface of leaves. These pores help plants in taking air in and out. Interact with senior class students in your school and request if they can demonstrate stomata using a microscope in your class. All living beings respire."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.285,
            0.576,
            0.883,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Have you noticed white patches forming on shirts around"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.606,
            0.424,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.148,
                0.606,
                0.424,
                0.87
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.182,
                0.882,
                0.396,
                0.9
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Water droplets on grass"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.44,
            0.596,
            0.884,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the armpits during summers? These patches are formed due to sweat. The sweat consists of water and salts removed by the body as waste products. Removal of waste products from the body is called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "excretion",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Urine is also formed as a product of excretion in animals. Do you know that plants also excrete? You may notice plants excrete excess water and minerals in the form of small droplets on leaves. For example, grasses and roses. All living beings excrete."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.441,
            0.841,
            0.883,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us look at another characteristic. What is your reaction if you unexpectedly step on a sharp object, such as a thorn,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
